	<item>
		<title>By: Helgaleena Healingline ('Aeostra')</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=191&#038;cpage=1#comment-9883</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Helgaleena Healingline ('Aeostra')]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 04 Oct 2011 03:42:36 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembranceproject.wordpress.com/?page_id=191#comment-9883</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[&quot;I&#039;m only a Pir,&#039; he said. So many times.  And he is my Pir. I am one of many, and there are many who share my Sufi name too, yet he welcomed us all and is still there for us, even if he didn&#039;t expect us to stay. 

The first time I saw Pir was at a wedding he conducted in a Chicago rose garden in 1979. It was so beautiful I could not stop weeping, which was a bit of an embarrassment during the dances of Universal Peace that followed.  Many years later I managed to &#039;keep it together&#039; enough in his presence at Camp des Aigles to take initiation. Even then he looked at me and said, &quot;Aren&#039;t you already an initiate of some other Order?&quot; and I had no idea in my head what it might be; I was much too busy staying in my body for the ceremony! Yet graciously he welcomed me in, and over the decades I was there for more instruction of his marvelous intellect and presence. 

So by a process of elimination over the rest of my life I have come to know what it was that Pir meant by this observation of my soul upon the mountain. Yet when I seek his darshan, he is still there for us, beckoning in the right direction, casting his wise glance. Thank you for being our beautiful Pir.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>&#8220;I&#8217;m only a Pir,&#8217; he said. So many times.  And he is my Pir. I am one of many, and there are many who share my Sufi name too, yet he welcomed us all and is still there for us, even if he didn&#8217;t expect us to stay. </p>
<p>The first time I saw Pir was at a wedding he conducted in a Chicago rose garden in 1979. It was so beautiful I could not stop weeping, which was a bit of an embarrassment during the dances of Universal Peace that followed.  Many years later I managed to &#8216;keep it together&#8217; enough in his presence at Camp des Aigles to take initiation. Even then he looked at me and said, &#8220;Aren&#8217;t you already an initiate of some other Order?&#8221; and I had no idea in my head what it might be; I was much too busy staying in my body for the ceremony! Yet graciously he welcomed me in, and over the decades I was there for more instruction of his marvelous intellect and presence. </p>
<p>So by a process of elimination over the rest of my life I have come to know what it was that Pir meant by this observation of my soul upon the mountain. Yet when I seek his darshan, he is still there for us, beckoning in the right direction, casting his wise glance. Thank you for being our beautiful Pir.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: Sara Farishta Perkins</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=191&#038;cpage=1#comment-8243</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Sara Farishta Perkins]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 21 May 2011 17:00:27 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembranceproject.wordpress.com/?page_id=191#comment-8243</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[I will never forget that moment at my initiation, when he looked deeply into my soul-eyes and he recognized me.  It was one of the greatest gifts I have ever received: to remember that we can remember our past and place it in the present with love and feel the pull of that grace right into the future, all at the same time. 
For this and many other moments I am eternally grateful. 
Sara Farishta Perkins]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I will never forget that moment at my initiation, when he looked deeply into my soul-eyes and he recognized me.  It was one of the greatest gifts I have ever received: to remember that we can remember our past and place it in the present with love and feel the pull of that grace right into the future, all at the same time.<br />
For this and many other moments I am eternally grateful.<br />
Sara Farishta Perkins</p>
]]></content:encoded>
