		<title>By: Shahabuddin Less</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=191&#038;cpage=1#comment-18</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Shahabuddin Less]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 17 Jun 2008 00:45:35 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembranceproject.wordpress.com/?page_id=191#comment-18</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Dear friends,

Today, June 17th, is the urs day (the anniversary of passing from this
world) of Pir Vilayat Inayat khan.
As I remember him I am filled with such love and admiration for his wonderful and painful life. He lived with all the limitations of the human being and the aspirations and ideals of a bringer of God¹s message. His whole life could be experienced by others when they were present to his glance.  That glance was cosmically powerful and lovingly tender simultaneously. Sometimes, if he was angry or upset at some injustice he
observed, the glance was full of fire. Sometimes the glance was so eagle-like one expected him to fly away. Sometimes when he thought of the tragedy of his sister and others he loved dearly the glance became deepened by God¹s sadness at the folly of human beings.

Pir Vilayat was a true friend and teacher who tried always to respect my freedom and yet shared his guidance in the deepest way.  He so desperately wanted his friends and mureeds to become all that was in their potential and experience the joy of incarnation: to have the courage to be all that the
universe envisions for each incarnation.

For so many of his mureeds he is closer today than ever.
Please take a moment and feel his glance within you today whether you knew him in this life or not.
Love and Blessings,
Shahabuddin]]></description>
